DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260224T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260224T213000
UID:71cfe6568a9b98b5f1258eb9@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:You can either learn to meditate from scratch and develop the 
 foundations for a daily practice or join the regulars to build on what you
  know and discover how to apply Wisdom reflections in meditation.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/tues-night-24-feb
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Foundations of Meditation Course
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260224T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260224T223000
UID:063f784063afcd4cf9f745e6@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Our mind is notoriously tricky - hard to manage\, mostly uncon
 scious\, creative and destructive by degrees. What’s crucial is to be ab
 le to work with this tricky ‘non-thing’ called the mind. Buddhism has 
 2\,500 years of experience working with the mind. In this sense\, meditati
 on is at the heart of Buddhism.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/foundations-of-meditatio
 n-course-feb-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daytime Buddhism & Meditation Class
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260225T103500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260225T123000
UID:0f9ce662a3269b8bda777adc@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:We will be examining the Ten Fetters\, the inclinations\, atti
 tudes and illusions we must break in order to gain full Enlightenment. Joi
 n in for our regular daytime weekly class of Dharma teaching and meditatio
 n. In person at the LBC and live on Zoom. There is also a crèche for thos
 e aged 6 months to 5 years old.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/daytime-buddhism-25-feb-
 ffc42
